<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ambon Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambon">Ambon</a> Island is an island in the Maluku archipelago of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, home to the city of Ambon, capital of Maluku province. Valued for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cloves">cloves</a>, it drew the Portuguese in the 16th century and was taken by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> in 1605, which made it the centre of its clove monopoly. Its northern Hitu peninsula long resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> control.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ambon-island.jpg" alt="Ambon Island" width="320" height="170" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lencer · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ambon_and_Lease_Islands_(Uliasers)_en.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
